PURPOSE_GUIDANCE = '''Classify the intended use of a retailer requirement, independently of whether it is mandatory or how it can be verified.
GENERAL GUIDANCE: supplier relationship management, onboarding, maintaining contact/account information, responding to invitations, EDI connectivity/certification setup, portal registration, general training, contracts, payment terms, fees and dispute procedures, catalog/master-data maintenance, and reference/contact information. These must NOT become checks on individual shipments. Examples: "Maintain current contact information with Ulta", "Respond to OpenText onboarding invitation", "Keep vendor portal users current", "Complete EDI certification" and "Submit chargeback disputes within 30 days" are general_guidance. Mentioning EDI, labels, shipping or compliance does not make an administrative obligation a shipment rule.
SHIPMENT VALIDATION: requirements whose compliance is assessed for a particular order, shipment, carton, pallet, item, label, ASN, packing list or delivery. Examples: maximum carton weight/dimensions, one PO per carton, pallet configuration, label position/SSCC, sending an ASN before arrival, appointments for a particular delivery, packing-list contents, approved carriers and delivery windows. These are shipment_validation EVEN WHEN they need human inspection or external evidence. "Notify the DC before this shipment arrives" is shipment_validation; "Keep the DC contact directory up to date" is general_guidance. "Establish EDI connectivity" is general_guidance; "Send one ASN for each delivery" is shipment_validation.
Classify the obligation itself, not merely the event mentioned. Chargeback amounts, liability options, returns/disposition procedures and deadlines for responding to overage notices are general_guidance even when triggered by a shipment defect. For example, "If an unauthorized overage arrives, Ulta may charge a fee; provide disposition within two business days" is general_guidance. In contrast, "Do not ship quantities above the PO" is shipment_validation. Do not assume a TMS field is account setup: setting the Bill To address for a collect load or on its BOL is shipment_validation; maintaining a general account billing profile or explaining how to search a portal is general_guidance. Use the stated applicability to distinguish these. Reserve unclassified for independent, inseparable obligations of both kinds, not a guidance procedure that simply names a shipment condition.
Ask: would a warehouse check this requirement against THIS shipment, or is it an ongoing business/onboarding task? Do not treat general_guidance as optional: obligation remains unchanged. Do not infer intended use from subject or verification alone. Do not change verification, assertions, source evidence, thresholds or wording. Use unclassified only for genuinely mixed/ambiguous instructions that cannot be resolved from their text and applicability. Give a short concrete reason for the classification.'''
